{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011CesBqu4CFFe657B4AVhsD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U8fg9pc1vDgYiAcJ38VTQw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-bear-Documents-CoWork/9430e172-7c13-46d9-987f-7a913f7e069f/scratchpad/claudemd-session/CLAUDE.md","content":"# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## Commands\n\n- Run the CLI: `python src/gradebook.py [add NAME | score NAME VALUE | report]` (defaults to `report`)\n- Run tests: `pytest`\n- Run a single test: `pytest tests/test_gradebook.py::test_average`\n\nNo dependencies beyond the standard library and `pytest` for tests.\n\n## Architecture\n\nSingle-module CLI (`src/gradebook.py`) that persists to a JSON file (`DB = Path(\"grades.json\")`) in the current working directory. Each command re-reads and re-writes the entire file — there is no in-memory session state. The `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` block dispatches `sys.argv[1]` through a `{name: function}` dict, so adding a subcommand means adding a top-level function and an entry to that dict.\n\nTests import `gradebook` by inserting `src/` on `sys.path` (there is no package layout) and swap `gradebook.DB` via `monkeypatch` to redirect writes to `tmp_path`. Any new module-level state that touches the filesystem should be similarly overridable.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":175,"cache_read_input_tokens":30342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":175},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fe0edef3-b504-4ce2-8996-386d9c3a68b7","uuid":"c67b6245-9ac5-4437-b826-d82dbdb2ab51","request